You can just write a method that takes your object and returns a DTO. There's no need for any framework to do that. For example:
public class Person {
    private String name;
    private int age;
    // getters and setters
}

public class PersonDTO {
    private String name;
    private int age;
    // getters and setters
}

public class PersonConverter {
    public static PersonDTO convert(Person person) {
        PersonDTO dto = new PersonDTO();
        dto.setName(person.getName());
        dto.setAge(person.getAge());
        return dto;
    }
}

This is the most basic way to do it. If you have a lot of classes, you can create a generic converter, but it's not necessary.
